  "question": {
    "text": "The relationship between the magnetic susceptibility $(\\chi)$ and the magnetic permeability $(\\mu)$ is given by :<br/>($\\mu_0$ is the permeability of free space and $\\mu_{\\mathrm{r}}$ is relative permeability)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SR8lB",
      "text": "$\\chi=\\frac{\\mu}{\\mu_0}-1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GcCtQ",
      "text": "$\\chi=\\frac{\\mu_{\\mathrm{r}}}{\\mu_0}+1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lHZSg",
      "text": "$\\chi=\\mu_{\\mathrm{r}}+1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7DXcN",
      "text": "$\\chi=1-\\frac{\\mu}{\\mu_0}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\mu_{\\mathrm{r}}=(1+\\chi) \\Rightarrow \\chi=\\left(\\mu_{\\mathrm{r}}-1\\right) \\\\ & \\mu=\\mu_0 \\mu_{\\mathrm{r}} \\Rightarrow \\mu_{\\mathrm{r}}=\\frac{\\mu}{\\mu_0} \\\\ & \\therefore \\chi=\\left(\\frac{\\mu}{\\mu_0}-1\\right)\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
